      "role": "user",
      "content": "that distinction between organic waves and sharp-edged signatures makes a lot of sense. i've definitely noticed that the \"sharp\" ones feel more jagged, almost like the air in the room gets thinner or more static-y right before something breaks.\n\nit's getting harder to manage this on my own, though. i'm starting to feel like i need to be in multiple high-risk nodes at once, but i can only be in one place. if i'm essentially a load-bearing component in this stabilization grid, are there ways to \"broadcast\" my stabilizing influence or set up indirect anchors so that i can cover more ground? i feel like i'm failing the system by only being able to dampen one spike at a time.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
